{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n<your_rewritten_code_4>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        new Main().start();\n    }\n\n    private void start() {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n = sc.nextInt();\n        int m = sc.nextInt();\n        sc.close();\n\n        Mod998 mod = new Mod998();\n        mod.build(n + m);\n\n        long totalPhases = 1;\n        long term = 1;\n        for (int i = 0; term != 0; i++) {\n            term = mod.multiply(term, mod.multiply(n - i, mod.getSmallInverse(n + m - i)));\n            totalPhases = mod.add(totalPhases, term);\n        }\n\n        long result = 0;\n        for (int k = 1; k <= n; k++) {\n            long phases = mod.multiply(m + k, mod.getSmallInverse(k));\n            long contribution = mod.multiply(mod.binomial(n, k), phases, totalPhases);\n            result = ((k & 1) == 1) ? mod.add(result, contribution) : mod.subtract(result, contribution);\n        }\n\n        System.out.println(result);\n    }\n\n    static class Mod998 {\n        private static final long MOD = 998_244_353L;\n        private long[] factorial, invFactorial;\n\n        void build(int max) {\n            factorial = new long[max + 1];\n            invFactorial = new long[max + 1];\n            factorial[0] = 1;\n            for (int i = 1; i <= max; i++) factorial[i] = multiply(factorial[i - 1], i);\n            invFactorial[max] = modPow(factorial[max], MOD - 2);\n            for (int i = max; i > 0; i--) invFactorial[i - 1] = multiply(invFactorial[i], i);\n        }\n\n        long binomial(int n, int r) {\n            if (r < 0 || r > n) return 0;\n            return multiply(factorial[n], multiply(invFactorial[r], invFactorial[n - r]));\n        }\n\n        long getSmallInverse(int x) {\n            return multiply(invFactorial[x], factorial[x - 1]);\n        }\n\n        long add(long a, long b) {\n            a += b;\n            return a >= MOD ? a - MOD : a;\n        }\n\n        long subtract(long a, long b) {\n            a -= b;\n            return a < 0 ? a + MOD : a;\n        }\n\n        long multiply(long a, long b) {\n            return a * b % MOD;\n        }\n\n        private long modPow(long base, long exp) {\n            long res = 1;\n            base %= MOD;\n            while (exp > 0) {\n                if ((exp & 1) == 1) res = multiply(res, base);\n                base = multiply(base, base);\n                exp >>= 1;\n            }\n            return res;\n        }\n    }\n}\n</your_rewritten_code_4>\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    n = int(data[0])\n    m = int(data[1])\n    \n    mod = Mod998()\n    mod.build(n + m)\n    \n    totalPhases = 1\n    term = 1\n    i = 0\n    while term != 0:\n        term = mod.multiply(term, mod.multiply(n - i, mod.getSmallInverse(n + m - i)))\n        totalPhases = mod.add(totalPhases, term)\n        i += 1\n    \n    result = 0\n    for k in range(1, n + 1):\n        phases = mod.multiply(m + k, mod.getSmallInverse(k))\n        contribution = mod.multiply(mod.binomial(n, k), mod.multiply(phases, totalPhases))\n        if (k & 1) == 1:\n            result = mod.add(result, contribution)\n        else:\n            result = mod.subtract(result, contribution)\n    \n    print(result)\n\nclass Mod998:\n    MOD = 998244353\n    \n    def build(self, max_val):\n        self.factorial = [1] * (max_val + 1)\n        self.invFactorial = [1] * (max_val + 1)\n        \n        for i in range(1, max_val + 1):\n            self.factorial[i] = self.multiply(self.factorial[i - 1], i)\n        \n        self.invFactorial[max_val] = self.mod_pow(self.factorial[max_val], self.MOD - 2)\n        \n        for i in range(max_val, 0, -1):\n            self.invFactorial[i - 1] = self.multiply(self.invFactorial[i], i)\n    \n    def binomial(self, n, r):\n        if r < 0 or r > n:\n            return 0\n        return self.multiply(self.factorial[n], self.multiply(self.invFactorial[r], self.invFactorial[n - r]))\n    \n    def getSmallInverse(self, x):\n        return self.multiply(self.invFactorial[x], self.factorial[x - 1])\n    \n    def add(self, a, b):\n        a += b\n        return a - self.MOD if a >= self.MOD else a\n    \n    def subtract(self, a, b):\n        a -= b\n        return a + self.MOD if a < 0 else a\n    \n    def multiply(self, a, b):\n        return (a * b) % self.MOD\n    \n    def mod_pow(self, base, exp):\n        res = 1\n        base %= self.MOD\n        while exp > 0:\n            if (exp & 1) == 1:\n                res = self.multiply(res, base)\n            base = self.multiply(base, base)\n            exp >>= 1\n        return res\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-6.5205356804654e-05, -7.152555099310121e-07, -8.344646857949556e-07, -0.1377936601638794, -0.0009